WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.245 --> 00:00:04.599
Is America headed for a civil war?

00:00:04.599 --> 00:00:08.525
According to the followers of one fast growing online subculture,

00:00:08.525 --> 00:00:15.341
increasing political polarization and instability will inevitably lead to a domestic armed conflict,

00:00:15.341 --> 00:00:19.440
which they refer to as Civil War 2, Electric Boogaloo.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.340
Electric boogaloo! The ultimate show.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:27.821
That's a play on the title of a 1984 break dancing film from which the movement known as the Boogaloo,

00:00:27.821 --> 00:00:32.804
aka Big Igloo, aka Big Luau, also derived its name.

00:00:32.804 --> 00:00:39.038
The Hawaiian shirt wearing gun toting activists known as Boog Boys have migrated out of meme space

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:44.388
and into the streets, showing up at Black Lives Matter demonstrations in many American cities

00:00:44.388 --> 00:00:46.960
in apparent sympathy with the cause.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:52.020
The media have called them white nationalists and accelerationist terrorists.

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:56.780
The Boogaloo movement is, for the most part,
a libertarian group, according to one member.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:01.180
But these labels don't capture what this dispersed
movement is all about.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:04.862
The Boogaloo movement is Gen Z second amendment
activism.

00:01:04.862 --> 00:01:09.314
It's members forego the patriotic symbolism of traditional militia movements

00:01:09.314 --> 00:01:12.741
for flowered apparel, bright patches, and colorful memes.

00:01:12.741 --> 00:01:17.450
Their approach to organizing resembles Hong Kong's decentralized, privacy-conscious,

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:19.920
and social media heavy protest movement.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:23.812
They're digitally native activists, raised on Instagram and Tik Tok,

00:01:23.812 --> 00:01:26.586
who understand that in the world of online feedback loops,

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:29.437
actions are often less important than the way they're presented.

00:01:29.437 --> 00:01:35.262
Their online rhetoric is infused with paranoia. And its members circulate unfounded theories

00:01:35.262 --> 00:01:40.747
of rampant pedophilia, which they say must be stamped out extra-judiciously if necessary.

00:01:40.747 --> 00:01:45.857
They claim that societal breakdown is inevitable, but their public stance often makes it seem as if

00:01:45.857 --> 00:01:48.903
a violent civil war is something they'd like to see happen.

00:01:48.903 --> 00:01:54.140
And the movement's organic leader-less structure leaves it highly susceptible to being co-opted

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:56.880
by its worst, most dangerous actors.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:03.560
The members that Reason spoke with stand against gun control, the drug war, and aggressive policing.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:07.139
We believe that everyone deserves to be free, quite simply,

00:02:07.139 --> 00:02:08.785
and we don't like federal government all that much.

00:02:08.785 --> 00:02:13.290
Sometimes they've aligned themselves with
right-wing militia groups, at other moments

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:14.650
with Black Lives Matter.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:18.820
The one issue that seems to unify them is
a conviction that armed resistance

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:22.460
to government overreach is entirely justified.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:24.870
They could tear gas us, but they ain't going
to tear gas us.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:25.870
You can try.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:27.240
I don't incite violence.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:29.060
I incite defense.

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:34.400
I would say it's a very powerful movement
that has come together and unifies against

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:38.020
racism, tyranny, pedophilia, government overreach.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:44.100
It's one of the biggest unified movements there has been among gun owner, freedom loving Americans.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:48.720
Mike Dunn has become a visible face in a mostly
faceless movement.

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:54.840
On October 8th, police arrested Dunn for allegedly
trespassing while open carrying a firearm

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:59.040
at a rally for libertarian presidential candidate,
Jo Jorgensen.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:02.700
You're telling me that you enforce the unconstitutional law.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:07.460
Dunn says he left home at age 16 and joined
the Marine Corps a year later.

00:03:07.469 --> 00:03:11.629
When he returned to Virginia, he embarked
on a new political project.

00:03:11.629 --> 00:03:15.519
The gun control push was getting really heavy
in Virginia and so I began building militias

00:03:15.519 --> 00:03:19.090
and connecting them all together under one head.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:26.680
Then my buddy, who I was connected with through
some militia work and online was Duncan Lemp.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:31.620
In March, Montgomery County Police shot to
death 21 year old Duncan Lemp

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:36.320
in his Maryland home after bursting in, in the middle of the night with an arrest warrant.

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:42.240
I believe they blatantly killed him in cold
blood and we were going to have justice.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:46.100
After he was killed, it really pushed me to
become part of the Boogaloo movement.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:51.800
Lemp's death gave rise to theories that he was targeted for his involvement with the militia movement.

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:56.720
Police say they were seizing firearms he wasn't
allowed to own because of a juvenile conviction.

00:03:56.730 --> 00:04:01.849
The Lemp faction of the Boogaloo movement
often use his name as a social media handle

00:04:01.849 --> 00:04:04.660
and regularly post about police brutality.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:08.900
While online racist groups speak of the Boogaloo as an impending race war,

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:12.340
this group portrays it as a sequel to the American revolution.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:16.680
Dunn says he was drawn to the movement by
its hard line stance against racism,

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:19.620
which set it apart from other armed movements.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:25.380
I had grown up country, flying the rebel flag,
saying some pretty dumb stuff and

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:29.240
that's something that attracted me to the Boogaloo movement was how much they hated racism

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:33.879
and how much they weren't willing to deal with it. And so I began changing some of my personal viewpoints

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:35.640
and began understanding things.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:39.540
Boogaloo members have marched alongside Black
Lives Matter protesters,

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:44.400
although their presence hasn't always been welcomed, and they've clashed with racist groups.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:49.200
The Boog Boys once led a chant of, "white
supremacy sucks," disrupting a speech

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:52.140
at a pro gun rally in Richmond. White supremacy sucks.

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:57.800
We're not white supremacists, we believe in liberty for all regardless of race, gender, whether you're trans.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:59.980
It doesn't matter, we need liberty for all.

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:04.539
John, who asked that we identify him only
by his first name, runs a Boogaloo themed

00:05:04.539 --> 00:05:08.080
Instagram page called too savage for statists.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:12.900
In addition to supporting Black Lives Matter, he was in Hong Kong in 2019,

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:15.000
helping pro-democracy demonstrators.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.340
He says there are parallels between the two
protests movements.

00:05:18.340 --> 00:05:22.060
How the Chinese media describes the Hong Kong
protestors...

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:25.900
Hong Kong was rocked by another violent clash
on Sunday.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:28.580
Again, between rowdy youth and police.

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:33.420
The exact same way the conservative media
in the US described the BLM movement.

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:38.380
A small group of highly aggressive, emotionally
charged activists took over our culture.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:41.560
They forced the entire country to obey their
will.

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:46.880
I don't think conservatives in America would
like to compare themselves to conservatives

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:49.460
in China, but that's really how it is.

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:53.190
I was worried that we would have seen more
violence directly attributed to the movement

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:54.710
than we have seen currently.

00:05:54.710 --> 00:06:00.580
Journalist Robert Evans coauthored an investigation
of the movement for the website Bellingcat.

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:04.700
He says the first time he noticed the Boog
Boys appearing at in-person events

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:09.380
was at the January 2020 gun rights rally in front of the Virginia State Capital.

00:06:09.389 --> 00:06:14.919
I began sort of after that point getting concerned
about what impact they were going to have

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:19.540
on the protests this summer, because obviously
2020, I've been expecting for a while,

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:22.340
was going to be a pretty harsh summer in terms of protests.

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:26.820
So the fact that there was this group of folks
who were kind of committed to the idea

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:29.340
of a societal breakdown and a civil war,

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:32.940
or at least committed to the idea of getting into gunfights with the police,

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:36.340
which was a big thing that I noticed in a lot of their early sort of memes,

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:40.660
that concerned me, which was why I started following them so closely.

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:46.760
No movement can tightly control its message, especially one as decentralized as the Boog Boys,

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:51.800
meaning anyone can easily carry out
violence and acts of terror under their banner.

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:56.820
One man accused of killing a sheriff's deputy
and federal agent in California had a Boogaloo

00:06:56.830 --> 00:07:02.289
patch in his car and allegedly scrawled Boogaloo
phrases in blood on the hood of a vehicle.

00:07:02.289 --> 00:07:06.900
The Department of Justice has charged three
men connected to the Boogaloo movement accused

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:12.220
of planning to incite violence with molotov
cocktails at a Las Vegas Black Lives Matter rally.

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:16.840
The FBI has even attempted to link Boogaloo
members with Hamas in order to charge them

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:22.740
under international antiterrorism laws, and
a federal law enforcement officer told NBC news

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:26.960
that some of the men involved in the plot to kidnap Michigan Governor Gretchen Whitmer

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:28.360
have ties to the movement.

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:33.100
I don't want to downplay the danger of this because you've got thousands of armed people talking about

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:37.660
wanting to contribute to a societal
breakdown.

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:43.040
Dunn and John both deny that they are actively
trying to accelerate domestic warfare,

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:47.620
but rather want to be prepared to resist a tyrannical government power grab.

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:51.409
In reality, nobody wants a war, nobody.

00:07:51.409 --> 00:07:55.760
We are prepared, but that's something we don't
want to happen.

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:58.920
At the end of the day, we don't need accelerationists.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:01.400
This is going to happen whether people want
to do or not, sadly.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:06.140
Mad Dog Mattis said something, "If you want to screw with me, please don't,

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:08.440
but if you do skrew with me, I will kill you all."

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:10.760
And I think that's the mentality of the movement.

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:15.880
But Evans thinks the fixation on collapse and violent conflict can become a self-fulfilling prophecy

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:22.960
as the presence of more armed civilians on the streets increases the likelihood of an inciting incident.

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:29.120
As someone who's reported from civil wars,
if they had a real physical understanding

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:34.580
of what civil war means and what it would
mean in this country, they wouldn't be buying

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:41.079
AR-15s and ammunition, they would be dedicating
their lives to stopping that from happening

00:08:41.079 --> 00:08:46.690
every single way that they could, because
there's nothing I can imagine that's more terrifying.

00:08:46.690 --> 00:08:49.060
Our founders put the second amendment in place.

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:51.200
The "armed people" was meant to be a check.

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:57.829
They wanted the people to be able to outgun
the state if they overstepped their bounds.

00:08:57.829 --> 00:09:01.920
The Boog Boys are only one of several armed
groups showing up at protests.

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:06.990
There are also the pro-Trump Proud Boys, which
drew media scrutiny after Trump's ambiguous

00:09:06.990 --> 00:09:09.720
statement about them in the presidential debates.

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:13.040
Proud Boys, stand back and stand by.

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:17.760
And there are black nationalist gun groups
like the Not F*cking Around Coalition,

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:21.880
and various militia groups like the Oath Keepers
and Three Percenters.

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:27.400
In the event of the predicted conflict between
warring political factions actually happening,

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:32.460
it's not entirely clear what side Boog Boys
like John and Dunn would align with.

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:38.520
Neither support Donald Trump or Joe Biden,
instead preferring libertarian Jo Jorgensen.

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:43.420
And in the field Boog Boys have often walked
a fine line, attempting to position themselves

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:49.680
as an armed buffer between police and demonstrators, peacekeepers between leftist and rightist groups,

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:52.026
as well as protectors of private property.

00:09:52.026 --> 00:09:55.360
That citizen was wrong and I'm all for protest,

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:58.339
but you can't be destroying your neighbor's houses and businesses.

00:09:58.339 --> 00:10:03.300
It's probably the largest actively armed movement
in the United States to date.

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:07.840
I know at one time we could have created a
Facebook group and had 100,000 people in it

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:08.900
that were dedicated.

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:14.460
We have groups everywhere, every state there's
Boogaloo Boys, so it is massive.

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:19.220
It is certainly the largest movement I have
seen in my lifetime in the United States

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:27.839
that is focused around armed citizens taking political action that focuses around those arms.

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:31.900
To understand the group's potential reach,
Evans says it's important to recognize

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:35.960
that apocalyptic narratives are deeply ingrained in the American psyche,

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:41.000
and that as principled as some of its members may sound, that the meme at the center of the movement

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:43.560
is still one of impending war.

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:45.960
How many Boogaloo folks are there? I don't know.

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:50.780
How many folks do I think are out there who
are interested in these ideas,

00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:56.660
and who are following these communities to some extent and who find this kind of conversation

00:10:56.660 --> 00:11:01.920
about what they will do in a civil war, and their excitement for said conflict?

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:04.480
I wouldn't be surprised if it was a couple
of million in this country.

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:08.500
I think one of the things that isn't done
enough, that you ought to do with talking about this,

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:13.300
is there's a direct line between the zombie apocalypse memes and stuff that were such a rage

00:11:13.300 --> 00:11:15.900
in the early aughts, and the Boogaloo.

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:20.940
That's where a lot of the people who are into this started buying guns, started buying arms,

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:22.440
started buying survival equipment.

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:28.240
More than anything what the Boogaloo has done
is taken that impulse and attached to it something

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:32.500
much more realistic because we're not going
to deal with zombies ever.

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:33.840
We might have a civil war.

